# IMP-01 (D-1, AC-001, AC-002, AC-004) the conversation window keeps the conversation's order: base, then the fix
# command: cd autobyteus-web && NUXT_TEST=true pnpm exec vitest run --reporter=verbose services/eventMonitor/__tests__/recentEventMonitorWindow.clockOrder.spec.ts
#          (first with recentEventMonitorWindow.ts from the base 1f761bc8db, then the fix; the file restored after)
# commit: base window file + the new spec; d67b58c740 (fix)
# env: macOS arm64, Node v22.23.1
# date: 2026-11-23
# result: Reproduced, then fixed. The base fails exactly the viewer-behind cases (4 of 9); the fix passes all 9. The
#         equal-clock compaction case passes on both: the tie rule is unchanged.
# The spec starts from the Solution Designer's reproduction (probes/clock-order-reproduction.spec.ts) and drives the real
# live handlers (handleMemberInputMessage with the node's received_at, handleSystemTaskNotification) with the viewer's
# clock set by fake timers.

## base window
 ok   the sender, the same clock: previous reply, You, the notice, the reply 3ms
